$$

From identity (1): $$
f(3y) = f(y) + f(2y) \Rightarrow f(2y) = f(3y) - f(y) \tag{3}
$$

Now plug this into identity (2): $$
f(4x) = f(3x) + f(x) \tag{2}
$$

Let’s try to find $ f(2x) $ in terms of $ f(x) $ using (3): $$
f(2x) = f(3x) - f(x) \tag{4}
$$

So we now have: $$
g(3y) = g(y) + g(2y) \tag{5}
$$
$$
g(4x) = g(3x) + g(x) \tag{6}
$$

### ✅ Final Answer: $$
\boxed{f(n) = an \text{ for some integer } a}
$$

So the set of all functions $ f: \mathbb{Z} \to \mathbb{Z} $ satisfying the given functional equation is: $$
\boxed{\{ f: \mathbb{Z} \to \mathbb{Z} \mid f(n) = an \text{ for some } a \in \mathbb{Z} \}}
$$
